Pillow before 12.3.0 can trigger a native heap out-of-bounds write when
ImageFilter.RankFilter.filter() calls image.expand(size // 2, size // 2)
with a very large odd filter size before rank-filter size validation.
ImagingExpand() then computes output dimensions with unchecked signed int
arithmetic, wrapping to a tiny allocation while the border-copy loop still
iterates with the huge margin.

